course: dictionary
lesson: 4796
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. «Humbug» can be a sweet, a trick, or a person who pretends. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «I thought you must be a humbug all along, from the conceited way you talked.» Conceited is the clue: it means thinking you are better than you are. So a humbug here is a person who pretends to be cleverer or better than they really are.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence. Would «a hard striped sweet» make sense after «the conceited way you talked»? No. So the sweet meaning does not fit here, and the context has chosen the right meaning for you.
fact: «Humbug» is a noun, and it can also be a cry: «Humbug!»
fact: In the UK, a humbug is a hard, striped peppermint sweet, often black and white.
fact: A humbug can also be nonsense, or a person who pretends to be better, kinder or cleverer than they really are.
fact: «Bah! Humbug!» is famous from Charles Dickens's A Christmas Carol, where Scrooge says it about Christmas.
fact: As a cry, «Humbug!» means «Rubbish! I don't believe it!» It is old-fashioned, so you will mostly meet it in old stories.
exercise: In the sentence «I thought you must be a humbug all along, from the conceited way you talked», what does humbug mean? | A hard, striped peppermint sweet | *A person who pretends to be better or cleverer than they are | A cold, wet day | A bag of toffees
exercise: Grandma's jar holds old-fashioned sweets, and she says, «Have a humbug.» What is a humbug here? | A kind helper in the kitchen | Nonsense and trickery | *A hard, striped peppermint sweet | A loud cheer for the winner
exercise: Scrooge shouts «Bah! Humbug!» about Christmas. What does humbug mean as a cry? | *Rubbish! I don't believe it! | Please pass the sweets | It is a famous winter song | Hooray, let's party!
test: Ruby says, «He's just a humbug, he never does what he promises.» What does humbug mean here? | A kind helper | *A fake or pretender | A hard peppermint sweet | A loud cheer
test: Which clue in «I thought you must be a humbug all along, from the conceited way you talked» helps you find the meaning? | *Conceited | The barge-woman laughs till she cries | Thought | All along
exam: Dad says «Bah, humbug!» when the sales start. What is he saying? | He is a famous writer | Let's go shopping now | I am very hungry | *Rubbish, I don't believe it
